--- List Slicing ---
[0, 1, 2]
[2, 3, 4]
[3, 4, 5]
--- String Slicing ---
Hello
World
--- Negative Slice Index (Supported) ---
Note: GladLang supports negative slice indices.
Positive slice: nums[1:4] = [20, 30, 40] (expected: [20,30,40])
Negative slice: nums[-2:] = [40, 50] (expected: [40,50])
Negative slice: nums[:-1] = [10, 20, 30, 40] (expected: [10,20,30,40])
Negative slice: nums[-3:-1] = [30, 40] (expected: [30,40])
All negative slice tests passed.
